1. Architecture Overview

1.1 Components
	•	Backend
	•	FastAPI application (HTTP API)
	•	Background workers (Celery or RQ)
	•	PostgreSQL (job metadata, results)
	•	Redis (task queue)
	•	File storage (PCAPs, intermediate JSON, reports)
	•	PCAP tooling (Zeek, tshark; Suricata logs from Security Onion)
	•	LLM HTTP client (calls local LLM endpoint)
	•	Frontend
	•	React single-page app
	•	Uses REST API for data
	•	Provides user-friendly UI for:
	•	Submitting jobs
	•	Tracking status
	•	Viewing reports
	•	External Systems
	•	Security Onion: PCAP and logs storage/API
	•	Arkime: PCAP/session indexing and export
	•	Local LLM: HTTP endpoint (Ollama / vLLM / LM Studio / custom container)

1.2 High-Level Data Flow

User / External System → FastAPI API → DB (Job) → Redis Queue
  → Ingest Worker → Parse Worker → Aggregate Worker → LLM Worker → Report Worker
  → DB (Result) → Reports (Files) → FastAPI API → Frontend / Caller


