4. PCAP → Clean Data Pipeline (Deterministic Steps)

4.1 Pipeline Steps

Given one job:
	1.	Ingest
	•	Save uploaded PCAP or fetch/export PCAP from Security Onion / Arkime.
	•	Store PCAP path(s) & related log paths in DB/metadata.
	2.	Parse & Normalize
	•	Run Zeek / tshark on PCAP:
	•	Produce JSON logs for connections, DNS, HTTP, TLS, etc.
	•	Parse:
	•	Zeek/tshark logs → FlowRecord[] and EventRecord[].
	•	Parse Suricata EVE logs (if available) → AlertRecord[].
	3.	Aggregation & Feature Engineering
	•	Choose time windows (e.g., 10-minute buckets).
	•	Compute:
	•	HostSummary[]
	•	HostPairSummary[]
	•	If both baseline and exploit ranges:
	•	Compute ChangeSummary[].
	4.	LLM Input Bundle Construction
	•	Build a bundle object:

class LLMInputBundle(BaseModel):
    exercise_id: str
    mode: str
    time_ranges: Dict[str, TimeWindow]  # keys: "baseline","exploit" or just "window"
    host_summaries_baseline: List[HostSummary]
    host_summaries_exploit: List[HostSummary]
    hostpair_summaries_baseline: List[HostPairSummary]
    hostpair_summaries_exploit: List[HostPairSummary]
    change_summaries: List[ChangeSummary]
    alerts: List[AlertRecord]


	5.	Chunking
	•	Compute anomaly score per ChangeSummary:
	•	e.g. sum of metric ratios + severity weights.
	•	Sort by anomaly score descending.
	•	Build chunk lists of top N entities (e.g., 3–5).
	•	Each chunk includes:
	•	Relevant HostSummary, HostPairSummary, ChangeSummary, AlertRecord.
	6.	LLM Calls
	•	For each chunk:
	•	Build textual prompt using system + user prompt templates.
	•	Call local LLM.
	•	Receive structured JSON response (see section 5).
	7.	Result Aggregation & Reporting
	•	Combine all chunk results.
	•	Produce:
	•	Global severity (max).
	•	Unique key findings.
	•	Combined MITRE TTP list.
	•	Host-level findings.
	•	Render final JSON JobResult.
	•	Generate Markdown & HTML reports.

